<InfoLayout title="About Auspicious Music" description="The purpose, expert roles, evidence boundaries and new ownership of the Auspicious Music Strings Lab." canonicalPath="/about/" lede="A new expert resource for viola, live strings, repertoire decisions and recording — built without borrowing the former site’s identity.">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">What this site is for</h2>
  <p>Auspicious Music now connects four decisions that are usually separated: what a viola or string part must do, which repertoire is feasible, how live music fits an event and how the instrument should be recorded. The core product is a practical planning layer rather than another broad music magazine.</p>
  <p>Das erste neue Werkzeug ist der <a href="/tools/eventmusik-planer/">Eventmusik-Planer</a>. Er macht aus Momenten, Einsätzen, musikalischer Richtung und praktischen Rahmenbedingungen eine Zusammenfassung, ohne Daten zu speichern oder einen Titel, ein Arrangement, einen Preis oder eine Buchung als bestätigt darzustellen.</p>

  <h2>Who is involved</h2>
  <p><a href="/authors/#kim-marie-borger">Kim-Marie Borger</a> is the named current viola expert. Her own site remains the source for current biography, recordings, repertoire examples and booking information. <a href="/authors/#matthias-ramahi">Matthias Ramahi</a> is the publisher and editor responsible for the website, source boundaries and corrections.</p>

  <h2>What is deliberately elsewhere</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Commercial booking pages, availability and offers stay on Kim-Marie’s own website.</li>
    <li>Photography and videography are not presented as Auspicious Music service clusters.</li>
    <li>Former downloads, catalogues, logos, identities and audience claims are not reused.</li>
    <li>Protected scores, lyrics, arrangements and recordings are not republished without documented rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The relationship to the former website</h2>
  <p>The domain previously hosted a different music-production website. The current site is a modern successor under new ownership, not a continuation of the former operator or catalogue. The <a href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">history and relaunch note</a> records the boundary and explains why unrelated spam URLs do not receive redirects into the new expert resource.</p>

  <div class="note"><p><strong>Launch safeguard</strong>Preview deployments remain blocked from indexing. A public launch still depends on final identity review and a rights-cleared starter set for any original media.</p></div>
</InfoLayout>
